---
/**
 * Terms and conditions: the English counterpart of `src/pages/terms.astro`.
 *
 * Same facts, same structure and the same effective date as the Bulgarian page,
 * including the awkward parts: the manufacturer's warranty, the limits of
 * liability and the fact that disabling emission systems is done ONLY for
 * machines that are not used on public roads.
 *
 * The Bulgarian page is the legally binding one; the first paragraph says so.
 *
 * The electric vehicles section has no English counterpart yet, so it is named
 * here without a link (no English page may link to a Bulgarian address).
 */
import Text from '../../layouts/Text.astro';
import { crumbSchema, bizRef } from '../../lib/seo';
import { BUSINESS as b, portalUrl } from '../../config/site';
import { LEGAL_EN, ROUTES } from '../../i18n';

const path = '/en/terms/';
const bgPath = ROUTES.find((r) => r.en === path)!.bg;
const [privacy, , , returns] = LEGAL_EN;
const portal = portalUrl('en');

const updated = '11 September 2026';
const address = `${b.address.streetEn}, ${b.address.cityEn} ${b.address.postalCode}`;

const site = Astro.site!.href.replace(/\/$/, '');
const schema = [
  bizRef(site, 'en'),
  crumbSchema(site, [{ href: '/en/', label: 'Home' }, { href: path, label: 'Terms and conditions' }]),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    url: `${site}${path}`,
    name: 'Terms and conditions',
    description: 'The terms on which PDK Tuning provides its services and on which the site is used.',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    dateModified: '2026-09-11',
    about: { '@id': `${site}/#business` },
  },
];
---
<Text
  title="Terms and conditions — PDK Tuning"
  description="Terms for using the site and the chip tuning, ECU software repair and dyno services: warranty, liability, legal limits and how disputes are handled."
  heading="Terms and conditions"
  lead="Who runs the site, what we take on, what we do not, and what we expect from you. Short and without small print."
  updated={updated}
  schema={schema}
>
  <p class="doc-binding">
    This English text is provided for convenience and has not been reviewed by a lawyer;
    the legally binding version is the <a href={bgPath} hreflang="bg">Bulgarian original</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {/* the company no. joins the sentence only when it exists; otherwise the sentence ends at the address */}
    The site is run by <strong>{b.legalName}</strong>, trading as {b.name},
    {address}{b.eik && <>, company no. (EIK) {b.eik}</>}.
    Contact: <a href={`tel:${b.phone}`}>{b.phoneIntl}</a>,
    <a href={`mailto:${b.email}`}>{b.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What these terms cover</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to the use of the site and to the services we arrange through it. By
    using the site you accept what is written here. If you disagree with something, do not use
    it and call us instead; things get sorted out faster on the phone.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information on the site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Catalogue figures are indicative.</strong> The power and torque values are read
      from our database and show a typical result for the engine in question. The actual result
      depends on the condition of the specific car, the fuel and the hardware.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Prices are starting prices ("from") and are not an offer</strong> in the legal
      sense. The exact price is given after an inspection or diagnostics and is confirmed before
      work begins.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The enquiry form is not an order</strong>; it is an invitation for us to get in
      touch. The only place on the site where you can order and pay is the electric vehicles
      section (currently available in Bulgarian only); prices there are final and points 4.1 to
      4.5 apply. Everywhere else on the site, prices are starting prices ("from") and are not an
      offer.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Booking, orders from the site, withdrawal and complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Appointments are made by phone or after an enquiry through the site. If you cannot come,
    call us. The dyno and the work bay are reserved for you, and an empty slot is lost for both
    sides.
  </p>
  <p>
    When the contract is concluded at a distance (by phone or through the form) or off business
    premises, as a consumer you have the <strong>right to withdraw within 14 days</strong> without
    giving a reason. There is one exception, and it matters: if you asked for the service to
    start within that period and it has been <strong>fully performed</strong>, the right of
    withdrawal no longer applies. The full procedure, with the deadlines, the form, the
    exceptions and how to file a complaint, is set out on the
    <a href={returns.href}>withdrawal and complaints</a> page.
  </p>

  <h3>4.1. What is ordered from the site</h3>
  <p>
    Through the electric vehicles section you order a package of <strong>two different
    things</strong>, and the difference matters for your rights:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The PDK Flasher device</strong>: a physical item that is delivered to you and
      remains yours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tuning software for your car</strong>: digital content made from the data read from
      your ECU and delivered through the app. It is not supplied on a physical medium.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Prices in the section are <strong>final, in euro, including VAT</strong>, and include
    delivery to an address in Bulgaria. For delivery outside the country, we agree the terms
    before confirming the order. A model without a published price cannot be bought with a
    button; you send an enquiry for it and the price is given after review.
  </p>

  <h3>4.2. When the order becomes a contract</h3>
  <p>
    An order sent from the site is <strong>your offer</strong>, not a concluded contract. The
    contract is concluded when we <strong>confirm</strong> it by phone or in writing. We also do
    this to check that the model and year match your car: the wrong ECU means a file that does
    not work.
  </p>

  <h3>4.3. Payment</h3>
  <p>
    Payment is by <strong>card or PayPal</strong>. It is processed by the payment service
    provider; we do not see or store your card details. If online payment is not available at
    the time of the order, the page says so and payment is arranged when the order is confirmed.
  </p>

  <h3>4.4. Delivery</h3>
  <p>
    The device is sent by courier to the address you give, usually within <strong>3 working
    days</strong> of the order being confirmed. The risk of loss or damage passes to you when you
    receive it. The software is not sent by courier; it arrives in the app after you have read
    the original file from the car.
  </p>

  <h3>4.5. Withdrawal from an order placed on the site</h3>
  <p>
    For the <strong>device</strong>, you have 14 days from receiving it. For the
    <strong>software</strong>, the right lapses if you have given express consent for preparation
    to start immediately and have confirmed that you thereby lose the right of withdrawal
    (Article 57, item 13 of the Consumer Protection Act (ZZP)). This consent is given with a
    separate tick box when you order and is <strong>never pre-ticked</strong>. If you do not
    give it, we wait for the period to expire before starting work on the file. Details are on
    the <a href={returns.href}>withdrawal and complaints</a> page, point 2.5.
  </p>

  <h2>5. The services</h2>
  <h3>5.1. Before any work</h3>
  <p>
    Every car goes through diagnostics. If the engine, turbocharger, injectors, clutch or any
    other part is not in a condition to take the change, we say so and do not write a file.
    Refusing to work on an unhealthy car is not poor service; it is how we keep it from getting
    worse.
  </p>
  <h3>5.2. The original software</h3>
  <p>
    The factory file is read and archived before any change. Going back to it is possible at
    any time. We keep the archive for the period set out in the
    <a href={privacy.href}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <h3>5.3. Legal limits</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Exhaust after-treatment systems (DPF/FAP, EGR, SCR/AdBlue) are disabled only on
    machines that are not used on public roads</strong>: competition, agricultural and
    industrial equipment. For a car that is driven on the road, we work on the repair:
    diagnostics, cleaning, replacing a sensor or a filter. The customer is responsible for
    truthfully declaring what the machine is used for.
  </p>
  <h3>5.4. The manufacturer's warranty</h3>
  <p>
    Changing the factory software may give an authorised dealer grounds to refuse warranty
    repairs on the engine and transmission. We warn about this before any work; the decision is
    the car owner's.
  </p>

  <h2>6. What we expect from you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>That you own the car or have the owner's consent.</li>
    <li>That you tell us about known faults, earlier changes to the software and replaced hardware.</li>
    <li>That the car is in working order, roadworthy and has enough fuel for a dyno run.</li>
    <li>That you do not ask for work that breaks the law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Warranty on our work</h2>
  <p>
    We guarantee that the file we write works as agreed. If a problem appears after our work
    and is caused by it, we fix it at no extra charge or restore the original software. The
    warranty does not cover damage from wear, poor fuel, later work by another workshop, or
    hardware changes made without our knowledge.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are liable for damage caused through our fault, up to the price paid for the service in
    question. We are not liable for lost profits, indirect damage, the consequences of incorrect
    information given by the customer, or events beyond our control (force majeure). These
    limits do not apply in cases of intent, gross negligence, or harm to life and health.
  </p>

  <h2>9. The partner file portal</h2>
  <p>
    Partner workshops upload files through a separate
    <a href={portal} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">portal</a> with its own
    registration. The terms published in the portal itself apply to it.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Acceptable use of the site</h2>
  <p>The following are not allowed:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>automated downloading of content (scraping) that puts load on the site or copies the catalogue;</li>
    <li>attempts to break in, get around the protection or overload the service;</li>
    <li>sending spam, advertising or malicious code through the form;</li>
    <li>using the brand, texts and photos without our written consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The content of the site (texts, photos, layout and catalogue data) is our property or is
    used with permission. Car manufacturers' logos belong to the respective manufacturers and
    are shown only to identify the make in question.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Personal data</h2>
  <p>
    How we process your data is set out in the <a href={privacy.href}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may change these terms. The new version applies from the moment it is published here;
    for a service already agreed, the terms in force on the day it was agreed apply.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    Bulgarian law applies. We try to settle any dispute by talking first. If that does not
    work, the court at our registered office has jurisdiction; if you are a consumer, the court
    for your current address has jurisdiction, as the law requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    As a consumer, you can refer the matter to the <strong>Commission for Consumer Protection
    (KZP)</strong>, 4A Slaveykov Sq., Sofia 1000, tel. 0700 111 22,
    <a href="https://kzp.bg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">kzp.bg</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For alternative dispute resolution (ADR), the competent bodies are the
    <strong>conciliation committees at the KZP</strong>:
    <a href="https://kzp.bg/pomiritelna-komisiya" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">kzp.bg/pomiritelna-komisiya</a>.
    The register of all recognised bodies in the EU is at
    <a href="https://consumer-redress.ec.europa.eu/dispute-resolution-bodies_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">consumer-redress.ec.europa.eu</a>.
  </p>
  {/*
    A LINK TO THE EUROPEAN COMMISSION'S ODR PLATFORM USED TO STAND HERE; IT WAS REMOVED ON PURPOSE.
    Regulation (EU) 2024/3228 repealed Regulation (EU) No 524/2013: complaints stopped being
    accepted on 20.03.2025, the platform was shut down on 20.07.2025 and the obligation to link
    to it went with it. Keeping the link is not just a dead link: pointing to a redress route
    that no longer exists reads as a misleading commercial practice. Do not bring it back.
    Directive 2013/11/EU (ADR) remains in force, hence the KZP conciliation committees above.
  */}
</Text>

<style is:global>
/* The binding-version note opens the body. */
.doc-body .doc-binding{color:var(--ink-3);font-style:italic}
</style>
